---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
const siteName = import.meta.env.PUBLIC_SITE_NAME || 'PetWellHub';
---
<BaseLayout title="About PetWellHub" description="PetWellHub's mission, scope, sourcing, and veterinary safety boundaries">
  <article class="container mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6 py-16 md:px-10 md:py-24">
    <header class="mb-12 border-b border-border pb-8">
      <p class="mb-3 font-mono text-[10px] uppercase tracking-[0.25em] text-accent">About</p>
      <h1 class="mb-5 text-5xl font-bold md:text-7xl" style="font-family: var(--font-display);">About {siteName}</h1>
      <p class="text-xl leading-relaxed text-foreground/70">Practical pet health and safety guides grounded in sources readers can inspect.</p>
    </header>
    <div class="prose-article space-y-8 text-[17px] leading-[1.75]">
      <section><h2>Our purpose</h2><p>{siteName} helps pet caregivers organize observations, prepare for veterinary conversations, and recognize when home monitoring should stop. The site does not diagnose pets, prescribe treatment, or replace a veterinarian-client-patient relationship.</p></section>
      <section><h2>What our sourcing means</h2><p>Public guides link to veterinary associations, veterinary schools and hospitals, regulators, public-health agencies, animal-welfare organizations, official product labels, and peer-reviewed research. A citation supports only the point for which it is used; it does not make every situation identical or guarantee an outcome.</p></section>
      <section><h2>No invented experience or review</h2><p>Articles do not claim hands-on product testing, patient outcomes, or professional review unless that work is documented and attributed. AI tools may assist research organization and drafting, but their use does not imply veterinary review or complete accuracy.</p></section>
      <section><h2>Safety comes before convenience</h2><p>Medication doses, insulin changes, treatment choices, and diagnoses belong with a qualified veterinarian. Collapse, breathing difficulty, seizures, suspected poisoning, severe trauma, inability to stand, or rapid deterioration require immediate veterinary or poison-control direction rather than an editorial email.</p></section>
      <section><h2>Corrections and contact</h2><p>Report a factual, source, accessibility, or safety concern to <a class="underline" href="mailto:editor@petwellhub.org">editor@petwellhub.org</a>. Include the page URL and the passage at issue so the concern can be assessed.</p></section>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
